# Local Sous Chef service for the HEADROOM measurement: the same binary that
# runs on int, pointed at the workstation's lab Ollama (127.0.0.1:11435,
# Ollama 0.34.4, speaks Anthropic /v1/messages) instead of Claude. No API
# spend. Used by `make -C lab headroom` after a Claude collection exists.
#
#   docker compose up -d --wait postgres          # repo root, Postgres on :5433
#   go run ./service/cmd/sous-chef -migrate        # with this env (or make build)
#   set -a; . lab/headroom.env; set +a; setsid nohup ./service/bin/sous-chef >> /tmp/souschef-headroom.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &
#   (detached: an eval of 76 cases × 8 outlasts a 2-hour agent task slot, and the
#   service must not die with it — measured 2026-10-04, one eval lost)
#   souschef-lab eval --url http://127.0.0.1:8091 --key local-headroom-key --route qwen9b …
#
PORT=8091
DATABASE_URL=postgres://souschef:souschef@localhost:5433/souschef_headroom?sslmode=disable
MIGRATE_AT_BOOT=on
SERVICE_KEYS=local-headroom-key
BUILD_ID=headroom

# No Anthropic route at all, so no key is needed. Routes speak the Anthropic
# Messages shape to Ollama; `stream:false` because Ollama's streaming frames
# differ. The *-ctx64k tags carry num_ctx 65536 (the prompt prefix alone is
# ~11k tokens of manifest index + ~26 KB of tools).
# Thinking: every route below runs with the messages-compatible default,
# "thinking":"disabled" (README §5) — the body says {"thinking":{"type":"disabled"}},
# Ollama renders the EMPTY <think> block (what the SFT rows contain) and stored
# thinking blocks are dropped from the re-sent history. Before 2026-10-04 the
# field was stripped, Ollama defaulted to think=true, and the base eval was
# measured with thinking ON — re-run the base eval before comparing an adapter
# against it (docs/LAB.md §6). Add "thinking":"enabled" to a route to measure
# the thinking-on variant.
MODEL_ROUTES='{"qwen9b":{"kind":"messages-compatible","url":"http://127.0.0.1:11435","auth":"none","model":"qwen3.5:9b-ctx64k","max_tokens":4096,"stream":false},"qwen27b":{"kind":"messages-compatible","url":"http://127.0.0.1:11435","auth":"none","model":"qwen3.8:27b-ctx64k","max_tokens":4096,"stream":false},"gemma31b":{"kind":"messages-compatible","url":"http://127.0.0.1:11435","auth":"none","model":"gemma4:31b-qat-ctx64k","max_tokens":4096,"stream":false}}'
# Candidate fields (README §5, docs/LAB.md §5): a messages-compatible route puts the
# <candidate_fields> block in the user turn unless it says "fields_context":"off".
# The three routes above therefore send it. An adapter trained WITHOUT the block
# (r2, r123: run.json has no fields_context, or enabled:false) must be measured on a
# route that says "off"; one trained with it, on the default. The lab asks the service
# which (GET /version states each route's fields_context; turn.done repeats it per turn):
#   souschef-lab eval --route qwen9b …   (--fields-context auto, the default; make eval)
# e.g. the same model both ways:
#   "blueberry-muffin":{"kind":"messages-compatible","url":"http://127.0.0.1:11435","auth":"none","model":"souschef-r123:q4_k_m","max_tokens":4096,"stream":false,"fields_context":"on","report_as":"blueberry-muffin"},
#   "blueberry-muffin-nofields":{…same…,"fields_context":"off"}
# ("report_as" = the id usage rows, traces and turn.done carry instead of the Ollama tag;
# the route name is free — the lab reads names and reported ids from /version and turn.done.)
#
# Hybrid (README §4, docs/LAB.md §6): "fallback" names the route a turn escalates to,
# at most once, when the student's op is refused, it reports unsupported, its call
# fails or it stops at max_tokens. The fallback must exist, differ, and have no
# fallback of its own; it need not be in MODEL_ROUTE_ALLOWLIST. With Claude as the
# fallback this file is no longer free: every escalated turn spends API money and
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY must be set (never commit it here). Replace MODEL_ROUTES with:
#   MODEL_ROUTES='{"blueberry-muffin":{"kind":"messages-compatible","url":"http://127.0.0.1:11435","auth":"none","model":"souschef-r123:q4_k_m","max_tokens":4096,"stream":false,"fields_context":"on","fallback":"default","report_as":"blueberry-muffin"},"default":{"kind":"anthropic","auth":"api-key","model":"<the Claude model id the int service uses>","max_tokens":8192,"effort":"medium"}}'
#   DEFAULT_ROUTE=blueberry-muffin
#   MODEL_ROUTE_ALLOWLIST=blueberry-muffin
# eval then prints the student-only pass, the hybrid pass and the escalation rate.
DEFAULT_ROUTE=qwen9b
MODEL_ROUTE_ALLOWLIST=qwen9b,qwen27b,gemma31b
MODEL_CALL_TIMEOUT=180s
TURN_TTL=15m
MAX_CONCURRENT_TURNS=2
TRACE_RETENTION_DAYS=90
